<title>ESTONIA: LOAN AND DEPOSIT INTEREST RATES RISE IN MAY.</title>
<headline>LOAN AND DEPOSIT INTEREST RATES RISE IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average long and short-term kroon denominated loan interest rates rose in Estonia in May, the country's central bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The central bank said in a statement that average kroon denominated loan interest rates were up to 12.7 percent in May compared to 11.2 percent in April.</p>
<p>Long-term average loan interest rates up to 10 years were at 13.3 percent compared to 12.5 percent for April.</p>
<p>Average fixed term deposits interest rates were higher in May at 4.5 percent compared to 3.8 percent in April.</p>
<p>--David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9201/2 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
